// Category: fatal errors — the run's outcome (exit code and error kind).
//
// A heuristic naming a tactic the theory never defines: proving dies with
// the tactic error, listing the `default` tactic HS falls back to;
// `@bound` shows the bound does not avoid it.
// No corpus theory fails this way.

// Category: proof corners no corpus proof reaches — a heuristic naming a
// tactic the theory never defines.
//
// The oracle evaluates rankings lazily: the `@bound` row cuts the proof at
// depth 1 before any goal is ranked, so it prints `sorry` instead of an
// error; the `@prove` row has to rank goals to replace the stored `sorry`
// and dies with "No tactic has been written in the theory file".  No corpus
// theory names a missing tactic.

theory MissingTactic begin
heuristic: {missing}
rule R: [ Fr(~k) ] --[ A(~k) ]-> [ Out(~k) ]
lemma open: exists-trace "Ex k #i. A(k) @ #i" by sorry
end
